* Building an Aztec wallet
** Unlike an Ethereum wallet
*** Private state lives in the wallet
*** The wallet proves (WASM, 10-60 s)
*** Every account is a contract
*** Fees before the first transaction
*** A view is a disclosure
** Components
*** Keys and accounts: Grumpkin key pairs, address before deployment
*** PXE: key store, note DB, simulator, hooks
*** Prover: proveTx, offscreen document
*** Pipeline: payload, fees, request, simulate, authwits, prove, send
*** Fees: Fee Juice, FPC, Sponsored FPC
*** Wallet SDK: discovery, P-256 ECDH, emoji check, capabilities
*** Approval UI
** Build order
*** Keys -> PXE -> deploy -> BaseWallet -> SDK protocol
*** Senders -> hooks -> backup -> fees -> own node
** Traps
*** Seed is not the whole backup
*** Scan before deployment
*** authorizeUtilityCall default denies
*** The node sees your tags
*** Service worker dies at 5 min
*** Oracle version, Sponsored FPC not on mainnet
** Wallets today (Sept 2026)
*** Azguard: extension, testnet
*** Obsidion: web, passkeys, Aztec Labs since May 2026
*** aztec-wallet CLI
*** EmbeddedWallet, tutorial extension
